' ===========================================================================
' FOLDERS.BM - the folders of the data files. Included at the end of
' CIVWAR25.BAS and CIVSET24.BAS.
'
' The DOS game kept every file beside the program. The port keeps them in
' folders of the folder the program starts in:
'   graphics\   the icons (.EGA) and the text screens (.SCR)
'   sound\      the sounds (.WAV)
'   data\       the campaign (CAMPAIGN.INI, REGIONS.INI) and the name lists
'               (.DAT, .LDR)
'   scenarios\  the scenarios (.CIV); the saved games, the PBM file and the
'               editor's new scenarios are written here
' The settings (PREFER.CFG), the history files (GENERALZ, MAXSKORS) and the
' campaign under way (REGIONS.SAV) stay beside the program.
'
' The Directory menu changes the current folder with CHDIR, and the game
' reads and writes the .civ files and the PBM file in the current folder.
' So setfolders makes scenarios\ the current folder, and every other file is
' opened by its full path, from the folder the program started in. The
' Directory menu then changes where the scenarios and saved games are, and
' nothing else.
' ===========================================================================

' Sets homedir$, gfxdir$, snddir$ and datdir$ (CIV20.BI), each with a
' separator at its end, and makes scenarios\ the current folder. Called
' first, before scriptstart, so that a script's CURDIR$ (scriptfolder$,
' SCRIPT.BM) shows scenarios\ as C:\CWB, as it showed the program's folder
' before the files were moved.
SUB setfolders
c$ = _CWD$
s$ = "/": IF INSTR(c$, CHR$(92)) THEN s$ = CHR$(92)
IF RIGHT$(c$, 1) <> s$ THEN c$ = c$ + s$
homedir$ = c$
gfxdir$ = c$ + "graphics" + s$
snddir$ = c$ + "sound" + s$
datdir$ = c$ + "data" + s$
IF _DIREXISTS(c$ + "scenarios") THEN CHDIR c$ + "scenarios"
END SUB
